A||||9||88FORMULA-T-TOP-GUY||Mr Mike's leather seats.  Opinions please.||||1||
Z||000000||88FORMULA-T-TOP-GUY||05-18-2001||07:09 AM||||My seats are shot and I am thinking of buying from Mr Mike's.  If you have first hand experience, please let me know your opinions regarding quality, looks, comfort, ease of instalation and if there are better, affordable options.  Thanks||||reg||1
Z||000001||Dan87GT||05-18-2001||07:51 AM||||I got a set of #8 Grey this winter, the seats are top notch. I had to sit in front of the TV/VCR and hit rewind several times for the first seat but it still only took me around 2 hrs, 2nd seat about an hour to recover. I have to say they fit perfect and look great, best money I've spent yet||||reg||1
Z||000002||FieroLisa||05-18-2001||08:56 AM||||I haven't bought any- YET. I haven't heard one bad thing about Mr Mikes though, and it seems that if you take it to any other upholstery shop its gonna be a heck of a lot more expensive.||||reg||1
Z||000003||mrfixit58||05-18-2001||09:26 AM||||Mr. Mike's are the best. This may sound a little funny coming from a guy who hasn't bought or installed a set but I do have reason. My mechanically challenged brother-in-law ordered a set for his 87 GT. He simply followed the step-by-step video tape instructions and in a couple of hours... beautiful seats. <P><BR><P>------------------<BR>Roy :D<BR>87 GT  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/pennocksize.JPG"> ||||reg||14
Z||000004||Alex4mula||05-18-2001||09:44 AM||||Have had them for 2 years. For leather in a Fiero look no further. He's the man. Have seen many types at Daytona show. All are excellent.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Oreif||05-18-2001||10:13 AM||||You are not going to find any better seats than Mr. Mikes. For quality, fit, cost, and ease of installation, he is the best. Most upohlstery places will carge $400-$500 per seat. The Fiero Store charges $375 just for the stock cloth SE/GT seats. For $25 more you can have Mr. Mikes Leather and in his kit he supplies <B>everything</B> you need. Including extra foam, and the tools to attach the seats!<P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/LOGO3.jpg">    <BR><B><I>Got Emblems?</I></B>||||reg||14
Z||000006||Black88GT||05-18-2001||10:23 AM||||Yeah I have been in the Fiero community for about 4 years or so and haven't heard one bad thing about Mr Mikes.  When I do my interior I am definitely ordering from him.<P>||||reg||14
Z||000007||Max The Chainsaw||05-18-2001||12:47 PM||||I just redid my first seat with Mr Mikes leather last week. (The car and the left seat are in the paint shop.) I'd recommend them to anybody. He even sent me extra material to fill in my speaker holes since i wasn't gonna reuse my speakers and didn't charge any extra. Quality was top notch, I'd say even better than Pontiacs....  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>You can't go wrong with his seats.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000008||Gumball||05-18-2001||06:07 PM||||I got my seat upolstered for only 300, in Genuine Mexican leather leather. I got it done at TJ.<BR>All i have to say is , neneer neneer neneer!<P>Viva Mexico!!||||reg||1
Z||000009||Ed||05-18-2001||06:51 PM||||I just today had another Fiero owner compliment me on my Mr. Mike's seats.<P>I highly recommend them in all aspects.||||reg||1
